NotesString/You can open this notes window for any project by selecting View->Notes...

This example shows activity on a USB 1.1 (Full Speed) port. 

You can see that polling is occurring periodically, with no activity in-between. 
Sample compression is especially useful in this scenario. Notice that this 
acquisition packed 804K samples into the sample buffer, providing nearly 
400:1 compression. This data was acquired at a sample rate of 200MHz. 
Zoom in near cursor A or B to see the resulting 5ns sample resolution.

You can easily zoom in to an area of interest by holding down the <CTRL> key
on the keyboard as you left-click with the mouse.

The interval between cursors A and B shows a typical 1ms USB 1.1 frame rate.

Notice that while USB uses differential signaling most of the time, it signals end
of packet (EOP) by pulling both lines low for two bit periods. Zoom in near cursor 
C or D to see an example.

Please note that all of the example files are "read only" so that they remain 
intact for future reference. You can change settings in these files for learning 
purposes, but the changes cannot be saved. You can however use the 
"Save As" option to save an editable copy of any example file./
